cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this dataset, please cite it as below, adding the version and
  release date of the release you actually used. Both are on the GitHub
  releases page and on npm and PyPI, and both packages export the matching
  DATA_VERSION constant.
type: dataset
title: "Algeria Wilayas, Daïras and Communes"
abstract: >-
  A complete, machine-readable dataset of Algeria's administrative divisions
  after the 2026 reform: 69 wilayas, 566 daïras and 1541 communes, with every
  name in Arabic, French and English, and postal codes for 1493 of the 1541
  communes. The hierarchy follows the ONS Code Géographique National, Loi 19-12
  (2019) and Loi 26-06 (2026). It is published as plain JSON, as an npm package
  and as a PyPI package, all built from one hand-edited source file and
  regenerated reproducibly. Records are never invented or interpolated: the 48
  communes with no available postal code ship as null and are listed in the
  documentation, and the 58-to-69 parent-wilaya mapping of the 2026 reform is
  not published at all, because it is not present in any source available to
  the project.
authors:
  - name: "El Amin"
    website: "https://el-amin.dev"
repository-code: "https://github.com/el-amin-dev/algeria-wilayas-communes"
url: "https://github.com/el-amin-dev/algeria-wilayas-communes"
license: CC0-1.0
# NO `version:` AND NO `date-released:` HERE, DELIBERATELY.
#
# Both fields are optional in CFF 1.2.0, and nothing in the release process
# updates this file: the version bump is owned by Changesets, which writes
# packages/js/package.json and CHANGELOG.md and never touches CITATION.cff.
# A hardcoded version therefore goes stale on the very next release and starts
# publishing a false claim in GitHub's "Cite this repository" panel.
#
# `date-released` was worse: it carried "2026-07-20", which is LAST_VERIFIED —
# the date the DATA was last checked against its sources. That is a different
# fact from when the software was released, and conflating them stated
# something untrue. If either field is ever reinstated, it must be reinstated
# with a mechanism that keeps it current, and `date-released` must be an actual
# release date. `LAST_VERIFIED` is exported by both packages and documented in
# docs/DATA_PROVENANCE.md; it does not belong here.
#
# A citation with no version is better than one with a wrong version. The
# `message:` above asks the citer to add the version they used.
keywords:
  - Algeria
  - wilaya
  - daira
  - commune
  - administrative divisions
  - postal codes
  - open data
  - geography
  - Loi 26-06
  - ONS
  - Arabic
  - French
  - JSON
